{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts","id":1071079,"title":"Homebrew 2e contracts!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-30T22:54:15-07:00","id":1071079,"title":"Homebrew 2e contracts!","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Let's swap stuff we've made!<br /> <br /> One of my players wanted to be a bard (more specifically, an anthropomorphic cello) for our campaign. I laid out of couple of ground rules, thinking it would be a changeling Merit. I realized though that it should probably be codified into a Contract.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>Orphic Hymns</i></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"> (\u2022 \u2013 \u2022\u2022\u2022, I might nudge this up a dot rating)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Changelings who were stolen away to Arcadia for their musical skills sometimes come back able to sharpen the senses or skills of others with their playing.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Cost</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">At \u2022, no Glamour to assist rolls involving Mental attributes (at Storyteller\u2019s discretion, music may help some mental tasks but may be disruptive to others)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">At \u2022\u2022, 1 Glamour to assist rolls involving Social and Mental attributes</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">At \u2022\u2022\u2022, 2 Glamour to assist rolls involving Physical, Social, and Mental attributes</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">At \u2022 \u2013 \u2022\u2022\u2022, spend 1 Willpower to only allow specific characters to benefit from the Contract (optional)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Dice Pool</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Dexterity (playing a musical instrument)/Presence (utilizing vocals) + Expression + relevant skill specialties + Wyrd</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Action</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Duration</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: One scene, or until the changeling is forced to stop playing</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Roll Results</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 Dramatic Failure: The listeners take dice penalties to their actions equal to the changeling\u2019s Wyrd. If used during combat, listeners also take the Insensate Tilt.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 Failure: The listeners receive no dice bonus, and the Glamour is wasted.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 Success: Successes are added to the pools of actions taken by all characters in listening distance.<br /> While playing in combat, the changeling can only move half their Speed (rounded down) during the turn. They cannot take any action that isn\u2019t evasive (excluding running, and including Dodging, which necessitates a Dexterity/Presence + Stamina roll after the double Defense roll to maintain playing continuity) without interrupting their play and having to cast the Contract again.<br /> Once per chapter, this Contract can be used to assist a First Aid/Intensive Care roll to heal or downgrade damage: 1 success per healed point of bashing damage, 2 successes per point of lethal damage downgraded to bashing, and 4 successes per point of aggravated damage downgraded to lethal.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 Exceptional success: The listeners gain the Inspired Condition. If the listeners already have the Inspired Condition due to this Contract, they gain the Obsession Condition alongside it and become hyper-focused on listening to the changeling's music.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Affinity Clauses</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">:</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 Darkling: The Darkling\u2019s music disperses through the air, as if coming from everywhere at once yet nowhere at all. If the Darkling passes a stealth check to hide in the shadows before using this Contract, they can add their Wyrd to all following rolls to remain hidden after they spend the Glamour for this Contract and begin playing.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2022 Fairest: The Fairest marshals their allies to greatness. They don\u2019t need to spend Willpower to prevent opponents from benefiting from this Contract.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 Ogre: The Ogre may use their Intimidation instead of Expression when using this contract. If they do, listeners take the successes rolled as penalties to their actions. On an exceptional success, the Ogre can inflict the Insensate Tilt to listeners. (This can be combined with the Fairest\u2019s clause to prevent specific characters from suffering said penalties as well.)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">\u2022 Wizened: After beginning to play, the Wizened\u2019s music can be heard through any obstacle as long as the physical distance between characters and the Wizened does not exceed the musical instrument\u2019s audible range.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Catch</span><span style=\"color:#000000\">: The changeling plays to drown out other instruments being played in their presence, whether by man or machine (i.e. an automated player piano or someone playing a harmonica, but not a radio or jukebox playing recorded music). The music <i>cannot</i> be from allies for the specific purpose of triggering the catch.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5236-lackey-man-ren","name":"Lackey Man Ren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T14:08:25-07:00","id":1071807,"title":"","content":"can we use this for questions about contracts too?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 04-01-2017, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T08:13:26-07:00","id":1072023,"title":"","content":"Don't see why not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5236-lackey-man-ren","name":"Lackey Man Ren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T10:42:35-07:00","id":1072089,"title":"","content":"Cool, then do you know if it's been said whether the first clause of Contract of Elements (Water/Freezing Water/Seawater/etc) protects you from drowning?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T00:20:12-07:00","id":1073604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1072089#post1072089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, then do you know if it's been said whether the first clause of Contract of Elements (Water/Freezing Water/Seawater/etc) protects you from drowning?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't <i>know</i>. I can take a stab at it, though.<br /> <br /> On one hand, &quot;gaining immunity to natural instances of the element&quot; in Cloak of the Elements seems pretty straightforward. On the other hand the Contract wouldn't necessarily protect someone from being <i>deprived</i> of an element out of the Contract's bounds (i.e. oxygen), in a &quot;it's not the fall that kills you, it's the landing&quot; sort of way. In this case, the fall and the landing in question are water and fatal hypoxia. I personally think that the Contract would protect well against torrential rain and blasts from a fire hose. At the same time, I feel it would not prevent a drowning death; this seems like the kind of infuriating loophole you'd find in a fae contract.<br /> <br /> Control Elements seems like a better choice for using water to prevent a watery demise. Controlling water to open a channel from the floundering changeling to open air sounds doable, but might require some penalties to the roll to reflect the pressure of trying not to drown!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5236-lackey-man-ren","name":"Lackey Man Ren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T00:31:44-07:00","id":1073607,"title":"","content":"It's times like these that Contracts are almost as creative as Mage Arcana in terms of application. And I definitely agree on those points for Control Elements and Cloak of the Elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T02:05:59-07:00","id":1073628,"title":"","content":"Creative indeed, since each Contract is essentially a Supernatural Merit with fairy tale motifs. The Seeming clauses make them even more varied.<br /> <br /> In fact, I have a hard time differentiating what would be a Contract, and what would be a (changeling) Merit. Anybody got ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T02:23:55-07:00","id":1073636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1073628#post1073628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creative indeed, since each Contract is essentially a Supernatural Merit with fairy tale motifs. The Seeming clauses make them even more varied.<br /> <br /> In fact, I have a hard time differentiating what would be a Contract, and what would be a (changeling) Merit. Anybody got ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it has multiple effects (to the point that some are reserved for a specific Seeming), it would be a Contract for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T14:57:28-07:00","id":1128206,"title":"","content":"Bumping this thread now that we know of the six Regalias and the nature of the division between Common and Royal Contracts. No ideas as of yet, though<br /> <br /> EDIT: Quote from the &quot;Contracts of Steed&quot; Preview<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Arcadian Contracts are broken out into categories called Regalia: Sword for strength and aggression, Shield for defense and protection, Crown for leadership and rulership, Jewels for manipulation and temptation, Mirror for perception and self-transformation, and Steed for movement both seen and unseen. </span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 08-12-2017, 08:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T16:56:38-07:00","id":1128255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1128206#post1128206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bumping this thread now that we know of the five Regalias</div> </div> </div> </div>Six. There's one for each core Seeming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T17:45:42-07:00","id":1128268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1128255#post1128255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Six. There's one for each core Seeming.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Woops, my mistake. Shall fix that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T12:41:14-07:00","id":1128918,"title":"","content":"This might be useful:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Changeling: The Lost, Chapter 7</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Contracts</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Common Contracts</b> are deals the True Fae originally negotiated for their servants. They focus on extending senses, and shaping what\u2019s already there, whether it be emotions or physical phenomena.<br /> <br /> <b>Royal Contracts</b> are agreements the Gentry originally forged for themselves, which changelings can make themselves party to. They deal with creating people, places, and things out of whole cloth, directly tampering with minds, forcing people to do your bidding, and affecting destiny.<br /> <br /> <b>Court Contracts</b> also come in Common and Royal categories. In this case \u201croyalty,\u201d rather than being those who rise to the levels of the Others, are those who rise to the level of the court founders.<br /> <br /> A Court Contract can be something that either the patron grants to the courtier, or that the courtier gives to the patron. For example, Summer grants a lot of heat-based powers, explained by such means as Helios being the lover of Summer and so well-disposed to her vassals. But Summer also grants powers which amplify wrath. Other Seasonal Contracts, such as Autumn\u2019s, provide ways for a changeling to consume the patron\u2019s emotions, feeding it. (Keep in mind that a \u201cpatron\u201d isn\u2019t necessarily a single entity or spirit \u2014 it just has to be able and powerful enough to make and uphold a deal with True Fae or changelings.)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Contract Creation</b></span><br /> <br /> To create a Contract, first decide whether it\u2019s more about manipulation or enhancement (and hence Common) or creating or wholly reforging (and therefore Royal). Once you\u2019ve established that, decide whether the Contract requires a roll to activate. Contracts that are actively resisted or opposed by other people should always require rolls, while Contracts that primarily affect the changeling or act on (apparently) inanimate objects should just work.<br /> <br /> Specific ranges of dice bonuses aren\u2019t as important as the nature of what the Contract does. Mind control that only lets you marshal someone the way that they were going is usually going to be Common, whereas one that stirs them to a grudge they\u2019d never before considered is usually going to be Royal.<br /> <br /> If the Contract belongs to a court, consider the court patron\u2019s personality and purview. Under most models, Summer\u2019s personality is fierce and unsubtle, and its emotions are anger and wrath. Therefore, Contracts that manipulate or create those emotions fit well. As well, Summer is a season of heat and dryness, so Contracts that summon scorching sunlight, or dry flesh to a crisp are also appropriate.<br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> A Contract can have almost any kind of effect. Most of them emphasize being tricky or slippery. Contracts, especially Common ones, usually provide a changeling with a way to \u201ccheat,\u201d rather than giving dominion over a broad mystical purview. However, Royal Contracts are usually a bit flashier than Common ones, and the powerful patrons or other forces behind Court Contracts can make their effects more overt.<br /> <br /> <b>Type of Roll:</b> Many contracts don\u2019t need a roll \u2014 if the changeling pays the Glamour or fulfills the Loophole, they just work. However, Contracts that are actively opposed often need a roll.<br /> <br /> The type of roll made to activate a Contract varies based on what forces push back against it and how success is measured. If another living or thinking force is acting against the Contract, and the number of successes matters, it\u2019s Resisted. Subtract one of the force's resistance Attributes from the player's dice pool.<br /> <br /> Where there's active resistance, but where the number of successes doesn\u2019t matter, the action is Contested. The opposing party rolls a Resistance Attribute + their Supernatural Tolerance.<br /> <br /> In either case, the player\u2019s dice pool is Attribute + Skill + either Wyrd (for Arcadian Contracts) or Mantle (for Court Contracts).<br /> <br /> <b>Loophole:</b> Every Contract has a Loophole, a way a changeling can get the Contract\u2019s benefits without spending Glamour or any other resource. It takes the form of a ritual behavior that appeases the patron in lieu of payment. The Loophole is always thematically related to the Contract, based on symbolism or sympathetic magic.<br /> <br /> For example, a Contract that protects against extreme temperature might allow a changeling to blow out a fading ember instead of paying Glamour. Even better Loopholes represent a small risk, like stealing a sentimental object from the target or forcing them to break your skin.<br /> <br /> The difficulty or risk of fulfilling a Loophole depends more on the value of the ritual to the other party in the contract \u2014 blowing out a candle lit by a true friend might be trivial for a changeling, but have great value to Intimacy itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 08-14-2017, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-14T12:54:18-07:00","id":1128929,"title":"","content":"Hmm, magic thats more about tricksiness than power....<br /> <br /> First thought is a Contract of Shield that lets you breathe anything that has oxygen in it. Oxygenated sea water, aerated dirt, even compounds that contain oxygen like h2o2. I'll stay it up later, but I'd peg it as Common<br /> <br /> EDIT: guess it could be a royal contract of mirrors that removes your need to breathe for a scene or a similar Winter Court Contract that puts you in suspended animation for [successes] day","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 08-15-2017, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T18:11:45-07:00","id":1131045,"title":"","content":"Recently dreamed up one idea for a powerful, expensive Contract: &quot;Spell of the Silver Screen&quot;<br /> <br /> It manipulates the minds of mortals so that they believe whatever outlandish things the &quot;director&quot; or &quot;actors&quot; do are part of a performance, movie shoot, or whatever. With an exceptional success, mortal bystanders (or victims) act 'in character' with whatever narrative the Changelings set up. An indirect cost is that it requires some &quot;setup&quot; in the form of costumes, faux camera crews, and the like to &quot;sell&quot; it. The spell breaks if a mortal actually gets hurt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T11:33:34-07:00","id":1135221,"title":"","content":"would you like to make a writeup of that one? Now that i'm back from vacation, going to try to write up my &quot;breath anything with oxygen&quot; contract<br /> <br /> <b>Everbreath (Common, Shield)</b><br /> <br /> The fae calls out to the spirits of air and life, drawing sweet breath from even the most unlikely of places<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 Glamour<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: None<br /> <br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Effects</b>: The fae makes a deal: Glamour for safe passage. For the rest of the scene, the changeling can breathe anything, solid, liquid or gas, that contains enough oxygen and nitrogen, whether oxygenated or made of oxygen-using substances. Thus, the character can breath water, dirt and even hydrogen peroxide as if it was clean air. This gives no buffs to movement speed, and she can still be choked manually.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental</b>: Closer to the elements than most, the Elemental can also bribe oxygen to avoid her enemies. For 1 Glamour, she can inflict the Thin Air Tilt on everyone but her within [Wyrd]+2 square yards for [Wyrd] rounds as an instant action and can reactivate this clause for 1 more Glamour as soon as the prior instance ends<br /> <br /> <b>Beast</b>: The Beast grows animal parts that allow them to move at their full speed in any loose solid or liquid environment, such as digging paws or fins.<br /> <br /> <b>Loophole</b>: the fae has taken care of a large plant or growing tree within the last 24 hours.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":".  EDIT: added Seeming Clauses 10-19-2017, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T12:25:54-07:00","id":1135243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1135221#post1135221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">would you like to make a writeup of that one? Now that i'm back from vacation, going to try to write up my &quot;breath anything with oxygen&quot; contract<br /> <br /> <b>Everbreath (Common, Shield)</b><br /> <br /> The fae calls out to the spirits of air and life, drawing sweet breath from even the most unlikely of places<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 Glamour<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: None<br /> <br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Effects</b>: The fae makes a deal: Glamour for safe passage. For the rest of the scene, the changeling can breathe anything, solid, liquid or gas, that contains enough oxygen and nitrogen, whether oxygenated or made of oxygen-using substances. Thus, the character can breath water, dirt and even hydrogen peroxide as if it was clean air. This gives no buffs to movement speed, and she can still be choked manually.<br /> <br /> <b>Loophole</b>: the fae has taken care of a large plant or growing tree within the last 24 hours.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you're asking about Spell of the Silver Screen, yeah, I'd like to see someone else write it up. I've been making it too big and complicated in my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T12:43:10-07:00","id":1135250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1135243#post1135243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> If you're asking about Spell of the Silver Screen, yeah, I'd like to see someone else write it up. I've been making it too big and complicated in my head.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, I'll try if you critique my contract first. quid pro quo","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T17:35:10-07:00","id":1135301,"title":"","content":"Everbreath seems pretty straightforward as a Contract. I don't know which Seeming is going to get Shield, but I can see a potential Beast perk that gives a movement bonus from fins or the like if they use Everbreath. Elemental would also be a natural choice for a Seeming that would benefit, like not needing oxygen in the medium at all.<br /> <br /> The loophole seems a little iffy to me, but it makes some sense, since trees provide oxygen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T18:41:20-07:00","id":1136038,"title":"","content":"Alright finally got around to this. Sorry for the wait. Feel free to critique.<br /> <br /> <b>Spell of the Silver Screen <i>or, the Fourth Wall Descends </i>(Royal, Mirror)</b><br /> <br /> The character weaves glamour into the very essence of their costumes and props as they make them, making them seem less real and more fantastical.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5 Glamour + 1 Willpower<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: Intelligence + Crafts + Wyrd; then Manipulation + Expression + Wyrd<br /> <br /> <b>Action</b>: Extended (12 - [Crafts+Wyrd] successes; 1 roll per hour) for creation; Instant for usage<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: Standard &quot;lose X successes&quot; for crafting roll. For the activation roll, this results in the Changeling being inflicted with the Delusional Condition as the magic overpowers even its own wearer's mind. Example delusions include, but are not limited to: an overpowering belief in narrative causality, believing they are acting out a scene and believing that they are a character in a story that resembles their current situation, such as thinking they are Inigo Montoya while crashing a Loyalist's wedding.<br /> <br /> <b>Failure</b>: nothing happens<br /> <br /> <b>Success</b>: The changeling, who can work with others for teamwork effects but must pay all glamour (but not Willpower) himself, creates a personal set of costumes and props that obfuscate their user's true supernatural abilities for 1 day. Any supernatural action performed by someone using these props is rationalized away by spectators as particularly clever special effects used in some sort of street performance or movie shoot, only so long as the Changeling succeeds on the roll, made whenever he first does something overtly supernatural in a Scene.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: Duration of effect extends to 1 week and targets temporarily act in-character as extras or chorus. This effect ends for anyone who is injured in any significant way while entranced.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental</b>: Drawing on her nature as a background feature, the Elemental can choose when creating the props to designate herself as &quot;crew&quot; instead of cast, penalizing Perception checks to notice her half her Wyrd rounded up<br /> <br /> <b>Grimm</b>: The Grimm can call on her nature as a living archetype to call down dramatically appropriate effects. For as long as the contract lasts, she may, once per scene, spend a Willpower to gain 2 automatic successes on a roll or subtract 2 successes from an opponents, manifesting as lucky or unlucky coincidences, so long as it is considered &quot;dramatically appropriate&quot; to the story they are portraying by the ST<br /> <br /> <b>Loophole</b>: The craftsperson breaks a hedgespun item they own and recycles it into the crafted set elements. This hedgespun item is subject to Sanctity of Merits<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":"plus, i'm thinking of removing the crafting roll and letting people resist the activation roll 10-19-2017, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T14:24:21-07:00","id":1136372,"title":"","content":"Nice. Using the costumes as a focus seems like a good way to do it, and this way, it seems like other supernatural beings could benefit from having a Changeling ally using the contract for them.<br /> <br /> Idea on the loophole: The Changeling sacrifices a Hedgespun item as an ingredient, which also extends the duration to the full week as if they rolled an exceptional success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T15:43:58-07:00","id":1136408,"title":"","content":"I like the loophole, but I think the secondary effect is a bit much. The way I see it, the exceptional success is the infused glamour being slower to leak out, not the effect of a larger Glamour supply. I'll put in my version in an edit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T00:45:10-07:00","id":1150922,"title":"","content":"I have Contract design that I suspect to be in 2e under different Regalia but let's give it a shot:<br /> <br /> Cloak of Mundane Banality (Steed, Common)<br /> Cost: 2 <br /> Action: Contested<br /> Dice Pool: Composure+Wyrd vs highest Composure within area or Composure + Supernatural Resistance of highest Potency individual present.<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> <br /> Roll Result: <br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: Contract fails but Glamour spend to activate it makes Changeling stand out from the crowd more. He takes [Condition].<br /> Failure: Contract fails.<br /> <br /> Success: Changeling conceals himself in oppressive sense of boredom that smothers any interest taken in him. People will ignore him as just another face in the crowd, taking penalty to perception rolls to notice him equal to successes rolled. Effect ends immediately if Changeling acts overtly out of place like steal something or move into restricted area.<br /> Exceptional Success: All perception checks to notice Changeling are reduced to Chance Die unless target spends point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> Beast: Can make activation of this Contract invisible to magic detection senses and instead make other magical effects stand out more within 20 feet of him.<br /> Wizened: Wizened can move freely around restricted areas, blending in with sanitary and low clearance staff.<br /> <br /> Loophole: Changeling has seen a stranger yawn within 15 minutes before activating this Contract.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T06:04:39-07:00","id":1150971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1150922#post1150922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have Contract design that I suspect to be in 2e under different Regalia but let's give it a shot:<br /> <br /> Cloak of Mundane Banality (Steed, Common)<br /> Cost: 2 <br /> Action: Contested<br /> Dice Pool: Composure+Wyrd vs highest Composure within area or Composure + Supernatural Resistance of highest Potency individual present.<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> <br /> Roll Result: <br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: Contract fails but Glamour spend to activate it makes Changeling stand out from the crowd more. He takes [Condition].<br /> Failure: Contract fails.<br /> <br /> Success: Changeling conceals himself in oppressive sense of boredom that smothers any interest taken in him. People will ignore him as just another face in the crowd, taking penalty to perception rolls to notice him equal to successes rolled. Effect ends immediately if Changeling acts overtly out of place like steal something or move into restricted area.<br /> Exceptional Success: All perception checks to notice Changeling are reduced to Chance Die unless target spends point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> Beast: Can make activation of this Contract invisible to magic detection senses and instead make other magical effects stand out more within 20 feet of him.<br /> Wizened: Wizened can move freely around restricted areas, blending in with sanitary and low clearance staff.<br /> <br /> Loophole: Changeling has seen a stranger yawn within 15 minutes before activating this Contract.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd put it under Mirror, which manipulates Perception. Also, for its Loophole, I'd say you have to -closely- observe them yawning, and it has to specificallu be from boredom, not fatigue. But that's just my opinion, since I love powers that encourage Changelings to cultivate strange and sometimes unsettling quirks. Glad to see someone on this thread again. Just realized I had no Dramatic Failure state for my contracts, any idea for that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T06:23:46-07:00","id":1150973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1150971#post1150971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd put it under Mirror, which manipulates Perception. Also, for its Loophole, I'd say you have to -closely- observe them yawning, and it has to specificallu be from boredom, not fatigue. But that's just my opinion, since I love powers that encourage Changelings to cultivate strange and sometimes unsettling quirks. Glad to see someone on this thread again. Just realized I had no Dramatic Failure state for my contracts, any idea for that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Jewels or maybe even Crown. This is basically Boredom Bedlam, not actual invisibility.<br /> <br /> Can you even get Dramatic Failure on extended action? <br /> Well you got second roll for activation so how about user getting Delusion Condition with their false belief being that they are in a movie?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":".  Correcting some embarrassing autocorrect mistakes. 10-19-2017, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T06:37:27-07:00","id":1150977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1150973#post1150973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think Jewels or maybe even Crown. This is basically Boredom Bedlam, not actual invisibility.<br /> <br /> Can you even get Dramatic Failure on extended activation?<br /> Well you got second roll for activation so how about user ghetto Delusion Condition with their false belief being that they are in a movie?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're right. I'm pretty sure when you a dramatic failure on an extended roll, it just subtracts 1 from your accumulated successes or something. That said, love that activation roll Dramatic Failure. How would it manifest though? Do they act like they think the Law of Narrative Causality is on their side or do they think they are normal human actors?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T06:49:59-07:00","id":1150980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1150977#post1150977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You're right. I'm pretty sure when you a dramatic failure on an extended roll, it just subtracts 1 from your accumulated successes or something. That said, love that activation roll Dramatic Failure. How would it manifest though? Do they act like they think the Law of Narrative Causality is on their side or do they think they are normal human actors?</div> </div> </div> </div>Leaving it vague would let each instance to be reinterpreted by players and Storyteller...<br /> That said yeah, we might want to brainstorm some examples. Blind faith in narrative causality, impaired judgement (such as wasting ammo and being confused at needing to reload), disbelieving all fae aspects of their life as plot of some movie they are making, or perhaps momentarily believing oneself to be a protagonist from a movie with similar situation (Motley tried to attack Privateer's wedding and now contract user is unable to tell apart reality from Prince's Bride)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12082,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","user":"Weird","date":". 10-19-2017, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T10:01:24-07:00","id":1151046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1150973#post1150973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you even get Dramatic Failure on extended action?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you choose to cause an extended action to dramatically fail for a beat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":18330,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18330-redspieder","user":"Redspieder","date":". 10-19-2017, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18330-redspieder","name":"Redspieder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18330_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T10:13:44-07:00","id":1151052,"title":"","content":"Not sure entirely what your asking due to the typos, but I think that would be a better question for the CoD Ask A Simple Question Thread, but yes, I think you can dramatic fail one of the rolls in an extended action for a beat","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T10:36:33-07:00","id":1151057,"title":"","content":"Well, I know you can chose to take a dramatic failure to gain a beat. Weird had said that he did not know if you could even get a dramatic failure on an extended action. I was just trying to bring up whether or not it was possible to choose to dramatically fail an extended action for a beat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18330-redspieder","name":"Redspieder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18330_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T10:48:41-07:00","id":1151060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1135221#post1135221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">would you like to make a writeup of that one? Now that i'm back from vacation, going to try to write up my &quot;breath anything with oxygen&quot; contract<br /> <br /> <b>Everbreath (Common, Shield)</b><br /> <br /> The fae calls out to the spirits of air and life, drawing sweet breath from even the most unlikely of places<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 Glamour<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: None<br /> <br /> <b>Action</b>: Instant<br /> <br /> <b>Effects</b>: The fae makes a deal: Glamour for safe passage. For the rest of the scene, the changeling can breathe anything, solid, liquid or gas, that contains enough oxygen and nitrogen, whether oxygenated or made of oxygen-using substances. Thus, the character can breath water, dirt and even hydrogen peroxide as if it was clean air. This gives no buffs to movement speed, and she can still be choked manually.<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental</b>: Closer to the elements than most, the Elemental can also bribe oxygen to avoid her enemies. For 1 Glamour, she can inflict the Thin Air Tilt on everyone but her within [Wyrd]+2 square yards for [Wyrd] rounds as an instant action and can reactivate this clause for 1 more Glamour as soon as the prior instance ends<br /> <br /> <b>Beast</b>: The Beast grows animal parts that allow them to move at their full speed in any loose solid or liquid environment, such as digging paws or fins.<br /> <br /> <b>Loophole</b>: the fae has taken care of a large plant or growing tree within the last 24 hours.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Bumping this to see people's reaction on the new clauses","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T10:49:52-07:00","id":1151063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redspieder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1151057#post1151057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I know you can chose to take a dramatic failure to gain a beat. Weird had said that he did not know if you could even get a dramatic failure on an extended action. I was just trying to bring up whether or not it was possible to choose to dramatically fail an extended action for a beat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> not the whole action, I think, but maybe one of the rolls. Also, I'm pretty sure you can only do that if you already normal failed the roll and the DM offers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T10:53:35-07:00","id":1151065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1151063#post1151063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> not the whole action, I think, but maybe one of the rolls. Also, I'm pretty sure you can only do that if you already normal failed the roll and the DM offers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> DUH! That's right, my mind just completely left that out. LOL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18330-redspieder","name":"Redspieder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18330_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T10:54:41-07:00","id":1151066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1150922#post1150922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast: Can make activation of this Contract invisible to magic detection senses and instead make other magical effects stand out more within 20 feet of him.</div> </div> </div> </div>About this. I assumed this was following the standard that conflicting powers always go to a Clash of Wills.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T14:58:36-07:00","id":1151118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1151066#post1151066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About this. I assumed this was following the standard that conflicting powers always go to a Clash of Wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, not my intention here. Just thought it be cool that the boredom wouldn't register as anything else but boredom, so Unseen Sense, Mage Sight, and Kenning (if it makes it into 2nd edition) would slip right past it. The secondary effect is just contrast making other magic seem more fantastic in comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T14:08:00-07:00","id":1153980,"title":"","content":"So I'm signed up for a 2e changeling game, playing a Darkling hitman for a court based on the Triads (in a free hold based on the various Mafia like orgainizations around the world. Italian, Irish, Chinese, Russian, and Japanese). When I first heard of Magic of the silver screen this sounded great! A contract that would like my knife fingered razor hand do his dirty work undetected, even walk out of the building in a blood soaked suit and have people just think they saw a film shooting...<br /> <br /> Then I read the whole thing and...not as useful to me as I would like. I think I need something a little different.<br /> What I need is a contract that makes people forget my face (ala laughing man from <i>Ghost in the Shell: Stand Alone Complex</i>). A contract that corrupts the memory of everyone who looks at me for a time. Let's see....<br /> <br /> <b>Sanguine Vissage Concealed (Shield - Common)</b><br /> The changeling calls out to nature of the Witness and demands to be shielded from their acusitions. Corrupting the memories of all who view them.<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Glamour<br /> <b>Dice Pool: </b>Presence + Stealth + Wyrd - Resolve + Tolerance. Use highest in group.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> Everyone notices you, and can remember every detail about you with uncanny clarity. +3 to recall or draw the changeling.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> Nothing happens, good luck.<br /> <b>Success:</b> Your face and identity are hidden from others. Those who look back upon their memories see you as if looking though a shower door, this effect lasts for 1 hour. This imposes a -3 on any attempt to recall or draw the changeling.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> The memories of those who looked upon you become so disjointed they don't just forget what you looked like but forget which way you were headed, the color of your clothes, or if you got into a car or rode off on a iron pony. Subejects gain the amnesia condition, effecting memory of you only.<br /> <br /> <b>Beast:</b> If the contract is a success your victims memories become even more scrambled and the remember you as an animal fitting for your Kith.<br /> <b>Darkling:</b> An excepeptional sucess happens on 3 successes rather than the standard 5.<br /> Loophole: The changeling paints their face in a victims blood before fleeing","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 10-30-2017, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T14:48:11-07:00","id":1153993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1153980#post1153980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sanguine Vissage Concealed (Shield - Common)</b><br /> The changeling calls out to nature of the Witness and demands to be shielded...</div> </div> </div> </div>Really interesting design but seems to be missing a loophole?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T16:17:26-07:00","id":1154009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1153993#post1153993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really interesting design but seems to be missing a loophole?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any recommendations? I'm not sure what would be a good loophole for a contract like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T19:35:57-07:00","id":1154042,"title":"","content":"I'd say making yourself really obvious. Like, smearing your face or your hand with the victim's blood, so that it's really obvious something's off if the Contract fails. I wouldn't disallow hiding the stains under clothing though.<br /> <br /> 3 more things. <br /> <br /> 1) Darkling clause is ridiculously OP. Change it to exceptional success atcl 3 successes<br /> <br /> 2) give all the effects mechanical effects, like a -3 to recall any identifying details about you on success, to giving them an temporary Amnesia condition related to anything your character did in their presence on exceptional success to making remembering details of the event a rote action on dramatic failure.<br /> <br /> 3) is it rolled individually against every witness or the highest dice pool in the area?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T06:31:05-07:00","id":1154113,"title":"","content":"I liked that loophole, and added it.<br /> <br /> 1)Modified the darling clause to match.<br /> 2) gave mechanics, used your suggestions since you. Seem to know what you are doing.<br /> 3) rolled against the heist in each group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T07:05:48-07:00","id":1154115,"title":"","content":"Getting better, but what about having the Penalties (and perhaps even the bonuses :3) scale with Wyrd, up to a max of 5 as is traditional. Also, I'd look up how the Amnesia condition works, and put some sort of either time limit or escape clause on it. The first is simpler, but the latter is very fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T12:34:06-07:00","id":1154803,"title":"","content":"I would suggest that rather than high risk high reward loophole proposed (the drawback of it is unlikely to ever kick in unless you mess up the roll), the Contract is specifically designed to protect ruthless criminals which means loophole is &quot;Regretful Criminal.&quot;<br /> <br /> Changeling doesn't need to pay for Contract activation if they are fleeting a crime scene with one or more negative mental conditions caused by their actions (say Guilty/Fugue/etc) or they had risked Clarity damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T12:36:04-07:00","id":1154806,"title":"","content":"I like that first part, but don't all murders risk Clarity Damage? You would never have to pay for the Contract. What do you think about the rest of my suggestions, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12082_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12082\" data-vbnamecard=\"12082\">Weird</a>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T13:44:37-07:00","id":1154829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1154806#post1154806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like that first part, but don't all murders risk Clarity Damage? You would never have to pay for the Contract. What do you think about the rest of my suggestions, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if murder will be Clarity breaking point or not since we aren't familiar with new Clarity rules...<br /> As for your suggest, the Wyrd penalty or bonus seems perfectly sensible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T14:58:26-07:00","id":1154852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1154829#post1154829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if murder will be Clarity breaking point or not since we aren't familiar with new Clarity rules...<br /> As for your suggest, the Wyrd penalty or bonus seems perfectly sensible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the general trend for the more human-like splats was to have murder always be a Breaking Point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T23:20:04-08:00","id":1156589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1154852#post1154852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought the general trend for the more human-like splats was to have murder always be a Breaking Point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't an assassin be virtually Immune to murder based clarity breaks by way of just becoming numb to it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T23:39:37-08:00","id":1156594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1156589#post1156589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't an assassin be virtually Immune to murder based clarity breaks by way of just becoming numb to it?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Murder, especially calculated is always Breaking Point. Theoretical Assassin could try to negate brunt of emotional stress by meditating before the hit and attending to therapy after payday but it would still be a breaking point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T23:51:00-08:00","id":1156596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1156594#post1156594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Murder, especially calculated is always Breaking Point. Theoretical Assassin could try to negate brunt of emotional stress by meditating before the hit and attending to therapy after payday but it would still be a breaking point.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xFA1UQ2UOVQ\" data-code=\"xFA1UQ2UOVQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/xFA1UQ2UOVQ/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> So basicaly this? Huh...a world of darkness full of Krombopulus Michael level of chill hitmen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T02:15:32-08:00","id":1156620,"title":"","content":"Fan Court Contract<br /> <br /> Touch of Shaper (Common, Court)<br /> <br /> Shaper Court, Court of Artisans and Visionaries prides itself as both explorers and inventors. No creation is more priced by Shapers than one created by inspired crafter and this Contract lets its user enjoy the benefits of inspiration.<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Cost: 1 Glamour + 1 Willpower<br /> Dice Pool: Resolve+Empathy+Mantle -Clarity (yes, it's easier to use when you are bit out of it.)<br /> <br /> Roll Results:<br /> Dramatic Failure: Changeling's attempt to reconnect with their inner muse fails miserably and their inspiration seeking focus turns toxic. Changeling gains Obsessed condition relating to seeing through creation of what they intended to build.<br /> Failure: No effect. Changeling must wait until next sunset or sunrise to try again.<br /> Success: Next Crafts/Computer roll Changeling makes to build/program something benefits from same bonus as if Changeling just cashed in an Inspired condition.<br /> Exceptional Success: As with success but roll also benefits from 8-again. In addition Changeling refills their Willpower as if they had fulfilled their Virtue.<br /> <br /> Loophole: Changeling intends to build their creation for a competition where it would be compared to similar works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T05:12:02-08:00","id":1156636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1156596#post1156596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xFA1UQ2UOVQ\" data-code=\"xFA1UQ2UOVQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/xFA1UQ2UOVQ/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> So basicaly this? Huh...a world of darkness full of Krombopulus Michael level of chill hitmen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nah, more like Samurai disturbed and troubled by the distance between their Buddhist and Shinto beliefs and all the death they deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T05:13:02-08:00","id":1156637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weird</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1156620#post1156620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fan Court Contract<br /> <br /> Touch of Shaper (Common, Court)<br /> <br /> Shaper Court, Court of Artisans and Visionaries prides itself as both explorers and inventors. No creation is more priced by Shapers than one created by inspired crafter and this Contract lets its user enjoy the benefits of inspiration.<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Cost: 1 Glamour + 1 Willpower<br /> Dice Pool: Resolve+Empathy+Mantle -Clarity (yes, it's easier to use when you are bit out of it.)<br /> <br /> Roll Results:<br /> Dramatic Failure: Changeling's attempt to reconnect with their inner muse fails miserably and their inspiration seeking focus turns toxic. Changeling gains Obsessed condition relating to seeing through creation of what they intended to build.<br /> Failure: No effect. Changeling must wait until next sunset or sunrise to try again.<br /> Success: Next Crafts/Computer roll Changeling makes to build/program something benefits from same bonus as if Changeling just cashed in an Inspired condition.<br /> Exceptional Success: As with success but roll also benefits from 8-again. In addition Changeling refills their Willpower as if they had fulfilled their Virtue.<br /> <br /> Loophole: Changeling intends to build their creation for a competition where it would be compared to similar works.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mind if I PM this to @Arcanea","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T06:18:38-08:00","id":1156654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1156636#post1156636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nah, more like Samurai disturbed and troubled by the distance between their Buddhist and Shinto beliefs and all the death they deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure those two concepts are at odds. Look at what Michael does before the collateral damage killings to get to his target. He was praying. Then he looks at a locket presumably at the picture of a loved one lost. But we assume they are dead, it could be they left him. We don't get too big an idea but these are likely two poles in his life.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a similar ritual would be in order for the loop hole. Spending 5 minutes in prayer and/or meditation then meditation on a object that connects you to earth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 11-07-2017, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T07:28:09-08:00","id":1156674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1156654#post1156654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not so sure those two concepts are at odds. Look at what Michael does before the collateral damage killings to get to his target. He was praying. Then he looks at a locket presumably at the picture of a loved one lost. But we assume they are dead, it could be they left him. We don't get too big an idea but these are likely two poles in his life.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a similar ritual would be in order for the loop hole. Spending 5 minutes in prayer and/or meditation then meditation on a object that connects you to earth?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nah, I like the current loophole. Let the Changeling deal with the emotional fallout themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T07:47:37-08:00","id":1156680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1156637#post1156637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Mind if I PM this to @Arcanea</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't mind at all. Go ahead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12082-weird","name":"Weird","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12082_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T10:10:04-08:00","id":1160243,"title":"","content":"Got another concept for a Contract a character of mine forged. Thinking about calling it something like &quot;Hacker's Script&quot; or the like. He can imbue a Contract or other fae power into a machine, letting it activate under predetermined condition, like &quot;Activate Touch of the Workman's Wrath on this gun if someone tries to shoot me with it.&quot; Or maybe other stuff like, &quot;Send this email if and when the Summer soldier breaks his pledge to me.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T16:39:28-08:00","id":1160356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1160243#post1160243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got another concept for a Contract a character of mine forged. Thinking about calling it something like &amp;quot;Hacker's Script&amp;quot; or the like. He can imbue a Contract or other fae power into a machine, letting it activate under predetermined condition, like &amp;quot;Activate Touch of the Workman's Wrath on this gun if someone tries to shoot me with it.&amp;quot; Or maybe other stuff like, &amp;quot;Send this email if and when the Summer soldier breaks his pledge to me.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like making a Pledge/Oath/Sealing with the object itself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T14:06:40-08:00","id":1183696,"title":"","content":"Not sure if this counts as homebrew, but if I wanted to update Discreet Conjuration, what Regalia would it fall under? A lot of its uses sound like Royal Mirrors, but then there's the part I love the most where you can just magically pull a small pistol or switchblade from your pocket, which sounds like Swords. Maybe making it a Goblin Contract could let it do both, but I'm not sure","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T17:00:44-08:00","id":1183765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1183696#post1183696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure if this counts as homebrew, but if I wanted to update Discreet Conjuration, what Regalia would it fall under? A lot of its uses sound like Royal Mirrors, but then there's the part I love the most where you can just magically pull a small pistol or switchblade from your pocket, which sounds like Swords. Maybe making it a Goblin Contract could let it do both, but I'm not sure</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it already exists as a more versatile Royal Crown Contract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-08T18:03:08-08:00","id":1183779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1183765#post1183765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it already exists as a more versatile Royal Crown Contract.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait, it does? Ok, one more reason I'm mad I missed the kickstarter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T23:11:16-07:00","id":1251572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1071079-homebrew-2e-contracts?p=1183779#post1183779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wait, it does? Ok, one more reason I'm mad I missed the kickstarter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know there was/is a after kickstarter thing where you can throw 20$~ for the early pdf. I missed the kickstarter too.<br /> <br /> Now my actual reply to the topic:<br /> <br /> Bottle Glamour<br /> Cost: 1 glamour<br /> Dice pool: None; Strength + Brawl + Wyrd vs Stamina + Wyrd<br /> Action: Instant; Contested<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> <br /> Effect: After spending the activation cost you may drain your or a willing creature's glamour into a container. <br /> If the creature is unwilling you may attempt a contested action and if successful drain a number of glamour equal to your wyrd. <br /> If you fail the ability fails to Manifest<br /> If you dramatically fail the power backfires and they instead drain you of glamour equal to their Wyrd. <br /> Loophole: The changeling prepares the vessel by swearing a pledge upon the item.<br /> <br /> With the rules of breathing new goblin contracts being basically goblins selling their abilities to changelings I thought this could be a useful ability to a changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T10:56:31-07:00","id":1375455,"title":"","content":"<u><i><b>Elvish Archery (Royal) [Sword Regalia] </b></i></u><br /> <i>The Changeling conjures a chimerical ranged armament out of thin air for the scene.<br /> <br /> Cost: 2 Glamour <br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> The armament has a Lethal Damage Bonus equal to Wyrd and its Ranges are [Wyrd x 10 / Wyrd x 20 / Wyrd x 40] in meters. It does not decrease your Speed or Initiative. Make a roll of Dexterity + Athletics or Firearms - Defense. To those who cannot see beyond the Mask, you appear to be using mundane armaments. The armament's Mien is influenced by Seeming, Kith, Court and Entitlement. You have a number of projectiles equal to [Wyrd x 10], and reloading takes an Instant Action.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Seeming Affinities</b></u><br /> <br /> Beast: Add your Wyrd to your Initiative. You can also move up to your full Speed reflexively once per turn and still make an attack.<br /> <br /> Darkling: If firing from behind at least Partial Concealment, you do not suffer penalties to fire back and receive 8 Again.<br /> <br /> Elemental: Your attack gains Armor Piercing equal to your Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Fairest: You can apply your full Defense against enemy shooters for a number of turns equal to your Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Ogre: Anyone who is hit by the armament immediately suffers the Frightened Condition, while surrounding enemies must roll Resolve + Composure - Wyrd or also become Frightened.<br /> <br /> Wizened: </i><i>You ignore the enemies' Defense.</i><br /> <br /> <i><u><b>Loophole:</b></u> The Changeling is wearing a trophy taken from a hobgoblin he hunted on the same day he activates the Contract.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-11-2020, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}